From 41ae82a01f5befa5bfc4492ae1eed705268ef4c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:34:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 278/283] feat(execution): add read-only U5 region planning
 (region plan + explain + CLI)

Promote a statically connected CoreProgram subgraph to a frozen, read-only
planning artifact, per the U5 region proposal 0020 section 1-2:

* plan_region(program, region_spec, policy, capability) supports the whole
  CoreProgram and explicit entry/exit boundary specs; raw op-index ranges are
  deliberately not part of the schema.  Invalid boundaries (dangling tensor,
  implicit capture, unused entry, unproduced exit, cycle, invalid Core IR)
  are refused with structured errors.
* REGION_SCHEMA_VERSION=1 document: boundary signature, topological per-op
  entries {opcode, contract_digest, single_op_plan_digest, provider_id,
  numeric_class, envelope|none}, region_digest =
  sha256(canonical(op digests + boundary signature + schema version)), and a
  region-level precision declaration composed by the conservative 0020 rules
  (no error cancellation, provider set always listed, per-op bounds summed
  with an explicit is-upper-bound statement).
* Unregistered opcodes are refused with an aggregated missing-contract list
  (opcode + occurrence count) so the batch-2/batch-3 registration order has a
  machine-readable input; registered-but-unrepresentable requests (scalar
  operand, unknown attribute) are reported separately and honestly.
* validate_region_plan/load_region_plan recompute the digest and the whole
  composition from the document alone and replay every op through
  plan_operation (two-way anchor); a rewritten document is refused.
* explain_region reuses the U3 per-op explain documents and adds a
  recomputable region composition derivation.
* CLI: plan --region / explain --region / explain --region-plan with the
  existing exit-code conventions (request errors -> 1, usage -> 2).

Read-only: no provider execution, no runtime import, no single-op path change
(plan_matmul/plan_qmatmul/plan_operation behaviour and digests pinned).

Tests: python/tests/ut/pypto_x/test_execution_region_planning.py (25 tests),
which errors on the parent commit because the region entry point does not
exist there.

(cherry picked from commit 46daf77d24a8533e0e4c1c6c0117f1c6cae01eb0)
